<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD JATS (Z39.96) Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v1.3 20210610//EN" "https://jats.nlm.nih.gov/archiving/1.3/JATS-archivearticle1-3.dtd">
<article article-type="research-article" xml:lang="en" dtd-version="1.3">
  <front>
    <article-meta>
      <title-group>
        <article-title>Cross-references, footnotes, and table rows</article-title>
      </title-group>
      <contrib-group>
        <contrib contrib-type="author">
          <string-name>Test Author</string-name>
        </contrib>
      </contrib-group>
      <abstract>
        <p>This abstract refers to <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig:elephant">figure 1</xref> and <xref ref-type="disp-formula" rid="eqn:euler">equation 1</xref>, with a
footnote<xref ref-type="fn" id="noteref-1" rid="note-1">1</xref>.</p>
      </abstract>
    </article-meta>
  </front>
  <body>
    <sec>
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p>A paragraph that references <xref ref-type="sec" rid="sec:intro">intro</xref> itself, plus
<xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig:elephant">figure 1</xref>, <xref ref-type="disp-formula" rid="eqn:euler">equation 1</xref>, <xref ref-type="table" rid="tab:demo">table 1</xref>, and
<xref ref-type="statement" rid="thm:pyth">theorem 1</xref>. It also has a foot-placed footnote
here<xref ref-type="fn" id="noteref-2" rid="note-2">2</xref> which collects
per-section, plus an endnote<xref ref-type="fn" id="noteref-3" rid="note-3">3</xref>.</p>
      <fn-group content-type="footnotes">
        <fn id="note-2">
          <label>2</label>
          <p>A foot-placed footnote in body text.</p>
        </fn>
      </fn-group>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Figures and tables</title>
      <p>A figure with a caption:</p>
      <fig id="fig:elephant">
        <label>1</label>
        <caption>
          <p>An elephant.</p>
        </caption>
        <graphic xlink:href="elephant.jpg"/>
      </fig>
      <p>A small CSV table whose rows render in JATS as <monospace>&lt;thead&gt;</monospace>/<monospace>&lt;tbody&gt;</monospace>:</p>
      <table-wrap id="tab:demo">
        <label>1</label>
        <caption>
          <p>A demo table with two rows.</p>
        </caption>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>a</th>
              <th>b</th>
              <th>c</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>1</td>
              <td>2</td>
              <td>3</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>4</td>
              <td>5</td>
              <td>6</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </table-wrap>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Math and theorems</title>
      <p>A numbered equation:</p>
      <disp-formula id="eqn:euler">
        <label>(1)</label>
        <tex-math><![CDATA[e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0]]></tex-math>
      </disp-formula>
      <p>A theorem:</p>
      <statement content-type="theorem" id="thm:pyth">
        <label>Theorem 1.</label>
        <title>Pythagoras</title>
        <p>If <inline-formula><tex-math><![CDATA[a^2 + b^2 = c^2]]></tex-math></inline-formula> then right-angled.</p>
      </statement>
      <p>A second footnote scope check<xref ref-type="fn" id="noteref-4" rid="note-4">4</xref>.</p>
    </sec>
  </body>
  <back>
    <fn-group content-type="endnotes">
      <fn id="note-1">
        <label>1</label>
        <p>An abstract-level footnote.</p>
      </fn>
      <fn id="note-3">
        <label>3</label>
        <p>A regular endnote.</p>
      </fn>
      <fn id="note-4">
        <label>4</label>
        <p>Section-scope footnote.</p>
      </fn>
    </fn-group>
  </back>
</article>
